      "updated": 1793545713951,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Dijikstra's Algorithm\n===================\n\n1. Mark the label of all the nodes to visisted by setting it to infinity .\n\n2. Update the source label to be 0 .\n\n3. For the current vertex , analyze all its adjacent unvisited neighbours and cal their label by adding the current label of the\ncurrent vertex to the weight of the edge that connects the adj vertex with the current node .\n\n4. Compare the recently measured with the current label assigned to the adj vertex and if it is leser then make it the new\nlabel .\n\n5. Consider all the unvisited neighbours of the current node and mark them as visted .\n\n6. If the destination node has been marked then finish .\n\n7. Find the minimum label , make it current vertex and goto step 3 .",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Dijikstra's Algorithm\n===================\n\n1. Mark the label of all the nodes to visisted by setting it to infinity .\n\n2. Update the source label to be 0 .\n\n3. For the current vertex , analyze all its adjacent unvisited neighbours and cal their label by adding the current label of the current vertex to the weight of the edge that connects the adj vertex with the current node .\n\n4. Compare the recently measured with the current label assigned to the adj vertex and if it is leser then make it the new label .\n\n5. Consider all the unvisited neighbours of the current node and mark them as visted .\n\n6. If the destination node has been marked then finish .\n\n7. Find the minimum label , make it current vertex and goto step 3 .",
      "autoResize": false,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    }
